From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:22:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: keep scratch buffers bound between batches, memoise
 the viewport

- The scratch buffer objects and the batch's attribute offsets stay bound from
  one batch to the next; a batch only points them at its data (vglBufferData).
  Blits, post passes and the overlay call client_arrays() before drawing from
  client arrays. Four GL calls fewer per draw, and vitaGL's vertex layout stays
  the same between batches.
- The viewport, scissor, flip, depth range and screen size of a draw are kept
  from the previous draw when the GE's viewport registers and the target are
  the same (230 instructions a draw on the Vita's CPU).
- The renderer trace prints each draw's texture, blend and depth state.
- docs/GL_RENDERER.md: "The CPU's share of a draw".

Verified: an old-versus-new replay of 328 frames over 15 cases (mission,
menus, movies, intro; scale 1 and 2; HD pack; --port baseline; --threaded) is
byte-identical to the build before b2e0cc3. Vita3K: mission 1 played 100 s
with the split renderer (the scratch-memory batch path), clean exit, menus,
cutscene and gameplay drawn correctly. Not yet run on a Vita.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

